model fx3
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.2 G1 (#211, plan §3): a def keyed by a movement depends on the movement (E §3.2), so its cell keeps the axes and the pins the movement reads. in_pln[t] reads t.cash.amount, which reads pay, which reads amt[work]: by_helper and in_pln[t] split by work (400.00 PLN under yes, 1 200.00 PLN under no), as by_inline does, never one line under [work = *]; and a pin of amt[yes] reaches the def (hp: 400.00, 2 000.00, 2 000.00 PLN). i is the stated twin, written inline; h3 the movements' amounts."

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
axis work
  yes "in work"
  no "not in work"
place wallet: accounts EUR lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input fx: num PLN/EUR
input d1: date
input amt[w in work]: money EUR
input mo: month

def pay: money EUR at reader
  rule base = amt[work]

move in1: transfers
  on d1
  at d1
  leg cash from world to wallet amount pay

def in_pln[t in transfers]: money PLN = round(t.cash.amount * fx, minor(PLN), half-up) at t.day

def by_inline: money PLN at reader
  rule base = sum(round(t.cash.amount * fx, minor(PLN), half-up) for t in transfers over mo where t.cash.to == wallet)
def by_helper: money PLN at reader
  rule base = sum(in_pln[t] for t in transfers over mo where t.cash.to == wallet)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  amt[yes] = 100.00 EUR "s"
  amt[no] = 300.00 EUR "s"
  mo = 2026-03 "s"
  fx = 4.0 "s"
  opening[wallet] = 0.00 EUR at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask i: by_inline law 2026-06-01
ask h: by_helper law 2026-06-01
ask h2: in_pln[t] for t in transfers over 2026-03 law 2026-06-01
ask h3: t.cash.amount for t in transfers over 2026-03 law 2026-06-01
ask hp: by_helper, by_helper as if {amt[yes] = 500.00 EUR}, by_inline as if {amt[yes] = 500.00 EUR} with work = yes law 2026-06-01
ask hw: by_helper, by_inline with amt[yes] = 500.00 EUR, work = yes law 2026-06-01
